        <mxCell id="ortho_text" value="ORTHOGONALITY PRINCIPLE: The five shock channels compose independently — 2³ × ∞² combinations (3 binary toggles × 2 continuous parameters). Each shock can be activated in isolation for sensitivity analysis, or combined into multi-shock scenarios (as in the Romania winter case study). The modular design means adding a new shock type requires only: (1) a YAML parameter, (2) an apply_* or add_* function in romania_winter_stress.py, and (3) a UI control in the dashboard." style="text;html=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=10;fontColor=#1E2B3A;fontFamily=Helvetica;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="76" y="758" width="1108" height="58" as="geometry" />
